# Khadas Edge1 - USB gadget (dwc3 on the USB-C port).
#
# AOSP's own system/core/rootdir/init.usb.configfs.rc does all of the work: it
# creates /config/usb_gadget/g1, the functions and configurations for every
# sys.usb.config combination, and binds the gadget by writing
# ${sys.usb.controller} to UDC. A device only has to say which controller that is,
# and that is a property, set in edge1_tv.mk alongside sys.usb.configfs.
#
# The dts decides the controller: rk3399-khadas-edge.dtsi gives usbdrd_dwc3_0
# (usb@fe800000) dr_mode = "otg" and usbdrd_dwc3_1 (usb@fe900000) dr_mode =
# "host", so the peripheral UDC is fe800000.usb.
#
# What this file used to contain could not work on a mainline kernel:
#
#   write /sys/class/android_usb/android0/f_ffs/aliases adb
#     android_usb is the pre-configfs gadget. It was removed from upstream long
#     before 6.12; the path does not exist.
#   setprop sys.usb.configfs 1, in "on boot"
#     init.usb.configfs.rc's actions are themselves gated on this property, so
#     setting it from an action is a race with the actions that read it. It is a
#     build property now.
#   two "on property:sys.usb.config=mtp[,adb]" handlers
#     They wrote the configuration string and nothing else - no functions, no UDC
#     bind. init.usb.configfs.rc already handles mtp, mtp,adb, ptp, rndis,
#     accessory and the rest; a partial duplicate only competes with it.
#
# So there is nothing left for this file to do. It is kept, and kept installed,
# because init.edge1.rc imports it and because the next USB question (an ADB-only
# gadget, or accessory mode for a TV remote) belongs here rather than in the
# board's main rc.
